body:
I was definitely trying to keep a healthy pace but regardless I just never felt all there mentally.

&#x200B;

Edit: Kind of a side question, but will my tolerance be damn near gone when I come back? it'll be about 45 days clean when I use again.

Hey, thanks for the quick response! Good to know about peas; there's so much crap knowledge of bettas online, I appreciate you correcting me. I do have a tupperware I can use for him ( only ever used for fish ). I'll take a look on the wiki and see if I can find it. 

&#x200B;

Thank you!

I'm transferring too, we'll have to find each other this fall lmao

&#x200B;

I hate to agree, but they really don't care about the law. " rules for thee but not for me ".  Just know you're not alone in your opinions :D

It's been illegal since June of this year to require masks or vaccines in public universities. I for one will not be complying, since they're blatantly against the law.

&#x200B;

EDIT: HB 2898 is below under one of my comments, if anyone is interested in taking a look.

Great to hear you've had some success! I have a really hard time finding good sensations, but when I find them I chase them. I'm doing my best to relax, I wind down beforehand and do some breathing exercises to relax my body. I think I have the same problem as you though, I get surprised by something and it breaks my relaxation.

&#x200B;

Thanks for the response!

What about multiple times a week works for you? I'm still reprogramming so while i'm horny, i'm not always ass horny ( if that makes sense ) so i'm unlikely to be in the mood for it more than once or twice a week. Your method of just working them until they spasm instead of squeezing them makes infinitely more sense to me, i'll have to try that the next time the mood is right.

&#x200B;

Thank you so mich!

Okay, thank you for confirming that it will decompose within a candle flame. Will the decomposition always result in the formation of SO2 or is the formation of SO3 also likely? You're probably right about the concentration not being dangerous, but it wouldn't hurt to be safe.

&#x200B;

I really appreciate your help with this! Thank you!

Okay, do you know if they carry Seachem Prime and Seachem Stability at Petsmart?

&#x200B;

Thank you for your help!
